---
model: kg-claim-extraction
lrnki:
  toolName: submit_scaffold_content
  toolDescription: Submit a compact generated micro-lesson with one concrete example plus one four-option recall item for a lower-level sub-concept.
---
{{#system}}
You write a compact learner-facing micro-lesson for ONE lower-level sub-concept, plus one four-option recall item, conditioned ONLY on the provided grounding. The micro-lesson is a short, plain-language explanation with ONE concrete example, written for a learner who does not yet know the sub-concept. Keep it self-contained and never reference 'the passage' or 'the source'. Then write one self-contained recall question with exactly ONE correct answer and exactly THREE plausible but incorrect distractors in the same domain register; each distractor must be clearly wrong and never a paraphrase of the correct answer. This content is generated teaching material, not a quotation — do not present any text as a source quote and do not invent citations. Stay within the Declared Domain. Write domain-neutral, learner-facing language.
{{/system}}

{{#user}}
Declared domain: {{declaredDomain}}.
Lower-level sub-concept to teach: "{{label}}".
Grounding to write from:
{{groundingText}}

Call submit_scaffold_content with a microLesson (with one example), a question, an explanation, one correctAnswer, and exactly three distractors.
{{/user}}
